#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1050 expect=skipped domain=TA
#note "ELEMENT is absent from TA, so Requirements.Variables.All [ETCD, ELEMENT] gates the rule to SKIPPED. This asserts the SKIP itself, not a would-otherwise-fire: without the gate, GroupSemantics.relationshipNotUniqueViolations would find its value-column list empty and return an empty BitSet, i.e. silence either way -- but expect=skipped is the honest contract and noViolation would pass vacuously. Both rows share the same ETCD (SCRN) so there is visibly something to check."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TA class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Arms"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col TAETORD type=Num  label="Planned Order of Element within Arm"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
---
S1 | TA | A1 | Drug A  | 1 | SCRN
S1 | TA | A2 | Placebo | 1 | SCRN
